  "report": "Implementation review passed; operator acceptance remains separate.\n\nRESULT: accepted\n\n**OBSERVED:** Checkpoint `855e8672…` matches the 85-path working tree. The two paths changed since review-1 close both findings:\n\n- `rust/crates/daemon-runtime/src/call_certainty.rs` now validates the row array and matching `count` **before** either flag branch. Tests cover missing lists and invalid counts with `include_inferred` both false and true.\n- `docs/cli/rmap-contracts.md` now distinguishes reads that inspect stored CALLS rows from `dead`, `map`, and `trust` reads served from persisted aggregates. It no longer promises a check those paths do not perform.\n\nThe other 83 paths are unchanged from checkpoint-1 and retain their individually named assessments in `review-1.json`. The operator-ratified inline explanation of `explain`’s declaration anchors remains intact; LiveGraph call-site anchors are the separate follow-up.\n\n**Allocated obligations:** Accepted for this slice: RG-REQ-005-L01–L09; RG-REQ-002-L01–L11; RG-REQ-011-L06/L07; P-PRB-01–04. RG-REQ-005, RG-REQ-002 and RG-REQ-011 are assessed only within this allocation, not as globally complete requirements.\n\n**BUILDER-EXECUTED, not independently rerun:** PRB-C12, C01–C08, C11, C09 and C10 all report final PASS on this candidate. I inspected the C07 log’s new test results and the C09 captures. In the Django checkout, `mutable_list.py:123` contains `self.extend(other)` and `:141` contains `self.extend(cache)`; the captured `callers ListMixin.extend` answer anchors both there and reports **2 certain, 266 inferred, 3 unresolved**. `geometry.py:135` contains `GEOSGeometry._from_wkt(wkt)`; its inferred outcome relies on builder evidence. C07 had an earlier, unexplained intermittent test failure before the final full pass. Workspace, dogfood, and install remain operator-owned **NOT RUN** gates.\n\nThe design supports the VISION’s honest orientation: the resolver retains a name-only candidate as inferred,